Run-length encoding of a string: each run of the same byte becomes a pair [count byte], and the pairs are the list of the runs in order.
The probe is a function that builds a list of pairs, with a nested recursive helper that counts a run and then hands the rest back to the outer function.
---
(lam s
  (letrec encode (lam l
      (if (? l) ~
          (let b (head l)
            (letrec run (lam r (lam n
                  (if (? r) [[n b] ~]
                      (if (= (head r) b)
                          ((run (tail r)) (+ n 1))
                          [[n b] (encode r)]))))
              ((run (tail l)) 1)))))
    (encode s)))
---
"" => nil fuel 200000
"a" => cons cons 1 97 nil fuel 200000
"aaab" => cons cons 3 97 cons cons 1 98 nil fuel 200000
"abba" => cons cons 1 97 cons cons 2 98 cons cons 1 97 nil fuel 200000
"zzzzzzzzzz" => cons cons 10 122 nil fuel 200000
"aabbbcccc" => cons cons 2 97 cons cons 3 98 cons cons 4 99 nil fuel 200000
